3:["$","div",null,{"lang":"en","children":[["$","$Le",null,{"lang":"en","items":[{"id":"001","slug":"distribution-is-the-moat","category":"doctrine","term":"Account-Generated Distribution","en":{"title":"What Is AGD Marketing? Account-Generated Distribution Explained","dek":"Everyone can produce. Almost nobody knows how to distribute. Welcome to the other side of the iceberg."}},{"id":"002","slug":"ai-sameness","category":"creative","term":"AI Slop","en":{"title":"AI Content for Social Media: How to Avoid Generic Output","dek":"Perfect faces. Interchangeable scripts. Creativity is not measured in exports per minute."}},{"id":"003","slug":"account-isolation","category":"doctrine","term":"Account Isolation","en":{"title":"Account Isolation in AGD: Build Distinct Social Accounts","dek":"Account Isolation: differentiate the voices before multiplying the profiles."}},{"id":"004","slug":"native-vs-api","category":"lab","term":"Native Posting","en":{"title":"Native Posting vs API Posting on TikTok: What Can You Test?","dek":"“APIs kill reach.” Here is the protocol that claim would need."}},{"id":"005","slug":"agent-first-dry-run","category":"machines","term":"Agentic AGD","en":{"title":"TokPortal MCP Tutorial: Preview an AI Workflow with Dry Run","dek":"A real MCP workflow starts with a readable preview, not a surprise charge."}},{"id":"006","slug":"multi-account-strategy","category":"doctrine","term":"Multi-Account Strategy","en":{"title":"AGD for TikTok 101: Accounts, Content and Your First Tests","dek":"A Multi-Account Strategy distributes a brand’s experiments across differentiated accounts."}},{"id":"007","slug":"content-isolation","category":"doctrine","term":"Content Isolation","en":{"title":"Content Isolation: How to Differentiate a Multi-Account Strategy","dek":"Content Isolation preserves meaningful creative differences between accounts: narrative, angle, format or purpose."}},{"id":"008","slug":"content-saturation","category":"doctrine","term":"Content Saturation","en":{"title":"Social Media Content Saturation: What It Means for AGD","dek":"Content Saturation describes content supply exceeding available attention."}},{"id":"009","slug":"feed-escalation","category":"doctrine","term":"Feed Escalation","en":{"title":"How AGD Changes the Competition for Organic Reach","dek":"Feed Escalation is our editorial term for intensifying formats, output and optimization inside feeds."}},{"id":"010","slug":"attention-war","category":"doctrine","term":"Attention War","en":{"title":"Organic Social Media for Apps: A StudyFetch TikTok Breakdown","dek":"A creator’s StudyFetch video moves from one awkward study problem to the actual app. Here is the structure an AGD team can use in its own product demos."}},{"id":"011","slug":"agd-not-phone-farm","category":"doctrine","term":"Phone Farming","en":{"title":"AGD vs Phone Farms: Strategy, Accounts and Infrastructure","dek":"Phone Farming describes infrastructure for operating accounts across mobile environments."}},{"id":"012","slug":"agd-without-tokportal","category":"doctrine","term":"AGD & infrastructure","en":{"title":"How to Build an AGD Strategy with Your Existing Tools","dek":"AGD is a strategy framework. TokPortal provides infrastructure that can support execution. A category that only works with one brand mostly looks like a campaign."}},{"id":"013","slug":"ten-principles","category":"doctrine","term":"AGD principles","en":{"title":"AGD Marketing Principles: A Practical Editorial Framework","dek":"AGD principles combine differentiated accounts, creative diversity, contextual execution and measurable learning."}},{"id":"014","slug":"anti-principles","category":"doctrine","term":"AGD anti-principles","en":{"title":"AGD Marketing Mistakes: Volume, Copying and False Promises","dek":"AGD anti-principles challenge clones, volume without diversity, certainty without data and averages without context."}},{"id":"015","slug":"native-account","category":"doctrine","term":"Native Account","en":{"title":"What Is a Native TikTok Account? Context and Limitations","dek":"In the AGD lexicon, a Native Account is created and maintained in the real consumer application environment."}},{"id":"016","slug":"account-persona","category":"creative","term":"Account Persona","en":{"title":"How to Build a Social Media Persona: The Duolingo Example","dek":"An Account Persona is the recurring identity that gives an account a perspective: who speaks, to whom, and why people return.."}},{"id":"017","slug":"hook-slop","category":"creative","term":"Hook Slop","en":{"title":"TikTok Hook Examples: Replace Clickbait with a Clear Payoff","dek":"Hook Slop means intense but interchangeable openings disconnected from the content’s actual value."}},{"id":"018","slug":"faceless-account","category":"creative","term":"Faceless Account","en":{"title":"Faceless TikTok Marketing: A Finch App Video Breakdown","dek":"Finch turns a seasonal challenge into a sequence of actions and goal cards. A practical look at faceless content that keeps the product visible."}},{"id":"019","slug":"formatted-account","category":"creative","term":"Formatted Account","en":{"title":"TikTok Content Series: Build a Repeatable Format","dek":"A Formatted Account uses a repeatable creative structure an audience can recognize."}},{"id":"020","slug":"chaotic-account","category":"creative","term":"Chaotic Account","en":{"title":"Duolingo’s TikTok Strategy: Character, Chaos and Continuity","dek":"A Chaotic Account allows several formats rather than one rigid template."}},{"id":"021","slug":"ai-persona","category":"creative","term":"AI Persona","en":{"title":"AI Personas for Social Media: Character Design and Disclosure","dek":"An AI Persona substantially uses AI for appearance, voice or production."}},{"id":"022","slug":"persona-agd","category":"creative","term":"Persona AGD","en":{"title":"Persona-Based AGD: Give Each Account a Distinct Voice","dek":"Persona AGD organizes a network around distinct editorial characters rather than generic brand accounts.."}},{"id":"023","slug":"slideshow-agd","category":"creative","term":"Slideshow AGD","en":{"title":"TikTok Slideshow Strategy: Story Structure for AGD","dek":"Slideshow AGD uses accounts publishing native carousels or slideshows."}},{"id":"024","slug":"story-slideshow","category":"creative","term":"Story Slideshow","en":{"title":"How to Structure a TikTok Slideshow as a Story","dek":"A Story Slideshow organizes a sequence around a situation and its resolution."}},{"id":"025","slug":"educational-slideshow","category":"creative","term":"Educational Slideshow","en":{"title":"Educational TikTok Content: Turn a Real Process into a Story","dek":"An educational slideshow communicates usable knowledge during reading."}},{"id":"026","slug":"meme-slideshow","category":"creative","term":"Meme Slideshow","en":{"title":"Brand Memes on TikTok: What Ryanair’s Persona Can Teach You","dek":"A Meme Slideshow builds its sequence around a cultural observation or punchline."}},{"id":"027","slug":"product-discovery","category":"creative","term":"Product Discovery","en":{"title":"TikTok Product Discovery: Lessons from the Ocean Spray Video","dek":"Product discovery content introduces a tool inside an understandable use case."}},{"id":"028","slug":"brainrotization","category":"creative","term":"Brainrotization","en":{"title":"Brainrot Marketing: When Internet Culture Helps a Brand","dek":"Brainrotization is our cultural shorthand for fast, absurd and compressed feed formats."}},{"id":"029","slug":"creative-brief","category":"creative","term":"Creative Brief","en":{"title":"How to Write a TikTok Creative Brief with a Concrete Example","dek":"An AGD creative brief connects audience, promise, format and hypothesis."}},{"id":"030","slug":"hook-payoff","category":"creative","term":"Hook & payoff","en":{"title":"TikTok Hooks and Payoffs: A Zach King Video Breakdown","dek":"The payoff is the narrative or practical answer to the opening promise."}},{"id":"031","slug":"creative-library","category":"creative","term":"Creative Library","en":{"title":"How to Build a TikTok Creative Library from Real Examples","dek":"A creative library organizes concepts, versions, rights and results."}},{"id":"032","slug":"format-fatigue","category":"creative","term":"Format fatigue","en":{"title":"TikTok Content Fatigue: When to Refresh a Recurring Format","dek":"Format fatigue is a hypothesis about weakening response after repetition."}},{"id":"033","slug":"creative-matrix","category":"creative","term":"Creative Matrix","en":{"title":"Creative Testing Matrix: Lessons from LEGO’s Instagram Reel","dek":"A creative matrix crosses variation dimensions: audience, problem, angle and format."}},{"id":"034","slug":"niche-warming","category":"field-notes","term":"Niche Warming","en":{"title":"TikTok Account Warming: Define a Relevant, Testable Routine","dek":"Niche Warming means exploring niche content in the app through searches, viewing and authentic interactions."}},{"id":"035","slug":"native-posting","category":"field-notes","term":"Native Posting","en":{"title":"Native TikTok Posting: Workflow, Features and Quality Checks","dek":"Native Posting means publishing through a platform’s consumer interface."}},{"id":"036","slug":"native-warming","category":"field-notes","term":"Native Warming","en":{"title":"Native Account Warming: Actions, Records and Limits","dek":"Native Warming happens in the real application through ordinary, authentic interactions."}},{"id":"037","slug":"geo-targeted-account","category":"field-notes","term":"Geo-Targeted Account","en":{"title":"US TikTok Accounts: Geography, Setup and Audience Limits","dek":"A Geo-Targeted Account is established and operated in its target market."}},{"id":"038","slug":"geo-posting","category":"field-notes","term":"Geo-Posting","en":{"title":"Geo-Posting for TikTok: Location Context vs Audience Targeting","dek":"Geo-Posting means publishing through an account operated in the target market."}},{"id":"039","slug":"us-launch","category":"field-notes","term":"US launch","en":{"title":"How to Reach US TikTok Audiences from Abroad","dek":"An international launch needs an understandable offer and a locally relevant use case."}},{"id":"040","slug":"localization-not-translation","category":"field-notes","term":"Localization","en":{"title":"TikTok Content Localization: Go Beyond Translation","dek":"Localization adapts meaning, references and uses."}},{"id":"041","slug":"account-brief","category":"field-notes","term":"Account Brief","en":{"title":"Social Media Account Brief: Audience, Voice and Publishing Rules","dek":"An account brief sets its promise, audience, voice and boundaries."}},{"id":"042","slug":"operator-handoff","category":"field-notes","term":"Operator handoff","en":{"title":"Social Publishing Handoffs: What to Give Your Operator","dek":"A handoff transfers an executable task with assets, constraints and success conditions."}},{"id":"043","slug":"publishing-window","category":"field-notes","term":"Publishing window","en":{"title":"TikTok Publishing Schedule: Plan Windows, Not Magic Minutes","dek":"A publishing window defines an acceptable interval for a task."}},{"id":"044","slug":"account-inventory","category":"field-notes","term":"Account inventory","en":{"title":"How to Organize a Multi-Account Social Media Inventory","dek":"An AGD inventory connects each account to its role, market, owner and observed state."}},{"id":"045","slug":"zero-views","category":"field-notes","term":"Stuck at 0 views","en":{"title":"Why Does My TikTok Have Zero Views? A Diagnostic Workflow","dek":"Stuck at 0 views describes low or absent distribution after publication."}},{"id":"046","slug":"shadowban","category":"field-notes","term":"Shadowban","en":{"title":"TikTok Shadowban or Low Reach? How to Investigate","dek":"Shadowban is an informal term for suspected distribution suppression without explicit notice."}},{"id":"047","slug":"distribution-failure","category":"field-notes","term":"Distribution failure","en":{"title":"TikTok Publishing Failures: Separate Upload, Access and Reach","dek":"A distribution failure can involve account access, a feature, removed content, a missing publication or weak reach."}},{"id":"048","slug":"native-not-deceptive","category":"field-notes","term":"Commercial transparency","en":{"title":"Organic Brand Accounts: Native Content and Transparent Identity","dek":"Content can be useful, native and commercial at once."}},{"id":"049","slug":"reddit-agd","category":"field-notes","term":"Reddit AGD","en":{"title":"Reddit Marketing and AGD: Contribute Before You Promote","dek":"Reddit AGD adapts account differentiation to legitimate community participation."}},{"id":"050","slug":"community-distribution","category":"field-notes","term":"Community distribution","en":{"title":"Community Marketing: How Brands Join Existing Conversations","dek":"A community is not merely an acquisition channel."}},{"id":"051","slug":"content-rights","category":"field-notes","term":"Content rights","en":{"title":"Social Media Content Rights: A Publishing Checklist","dek":"A provenance register connects images, sounds and videos to their origins and checked usage conditions."}},{"id":"052","slug":"campaign-retrospective","category":"field-notes","term":"Campaign retrospective","en":{"title":"AGD Campaign Review: Creative, Distribution and Evidence","dek":"An AGD retrospective connects objectives, execution, observations and decisions."}},{"id":"053","slug":"budget-of-learning","category":"field-notes","term":"Learning budget","en":{"title":"How to Budget an AGD Experiment: Costs and Learning Goals","dek":"A learning budget includes production, coordination, execution and analysis."}},{"id":"054","slug":"viral-hit","category":"lab","term":"Viral Hit","en":{"title":"What Counts as a Viral TikTok? Define the Comparison","dek":"A Viral Hit is an unusually high distribution outcome relative to a defined baseline: account, cohort or campaign."}},{"id":"055","slug":"viral-hit-rate","category":"lab","term":"Viral Hit Rate","en":{"title":"TikTok Viral Hit Rate: Define Attempts and Measure Outcomes","dek":"Viral Hit Rate is the proportion of eligible posts exceeding a predefined outlier threshold."}},{"id":"056","slug":"median-vs-mean","category":"lab","term":"Median vs mean","en":{"title":"TikTok Analytics: Average vs Median Views Explained","dek":"The mean adds values and divides by their count."}},{"id":"057","slug":"percentiles","category":"lab","term":"Distribution percentiles","en":{"title":"Social Media Analytics: How to Read Performance Percentiles","dek":"A percentile locates a value in an ordered distribution."}},{"id":"058","slug":"power-law","category":"lab","term":"Distribution concentration","en":{"title":"Why a Few TikTok Posts Can Dominate Your Reach","dek":"Concentration measures the share of outcomes produced by a fraction of posts."}},{"id":"059","slug":"top-ten-accounts","category":"lab","term":"Account concentration","en":{"title":"Multi-Account Analytics: Measure Performance Concentration","dek":"Account concentration shows which assets carry the total outcome."}},{"id":"060","slug":"matched-cohorts","category":"lab","term":"Matched cohorts","en":{"title":"How to Compare TikTok Campaigns with Matched Cohorts","dek":"A matched cohort aligns observations on known characteristics."}},{"id":"061","slug":"posting-time-myth","category":"lab","term":"Posting-time myth","en":{"title":"Best Time to Post on TikTok? Test Timing Without the Myths","dek":"Posting-time effects may depend on audience and context."}},{"id":"062","slug":"posting-frequency","category":"lab","term":"Posting frequency","en":{"title":"How Often Should You Post on TikTok? Design a Useful Test","dek":"A frequency test must separate total volume, per-post performance and production load."}},{"id":"063","slug":"warming-study","category":"lab","term":"Warming protocol","en":{"title":"Does TikTok Account Warming Work? An Experiment Protocol","dek":"A warming protocol compares preparations defined before publishing."}},{"id":"064","slug":"account-age","category":"lab","term":"Account age","en":{"title":"Does TikTok Account Age Affect Reach? What to Compare","dek":"Account age can be associated with history, followers and behavior."}},{"id":"065","slug":"slideshow-vs-video","category":"lab","term":"Slideshow vs video","en":{"title":"TikTok Slideshows vs Videos: How to Compare the Formats","dek":"Comparing slideshow and video requires a comparable promise and audience."}},{"id":"066","slug":"formatted-vs-chaotic","category":"lab","term":"Formatted vs chaotic","en":{"title":"TikTok Content Strategy: Recurring Series vs Spontaneous Posts","dek":"A Formatted versus Chaotic test compares a recurring structure with multiple formats."}},{"id":"067","slug":"creative-diversity-test","category":"lab","term":"Creative diversity","en":{"title":"TikTok Creative Testing: Compare Ideas, Not Just Edits","dek":"A creative-diversity test examines meaningful variation rather than counting files."}},{"id":"068","slug":"native-features-test","category":"lab","term":"Native features","en":{"title":"TikTok Native Features: Test Their Creative Contribution","dek":"A native-feature test separates a feature’s effect from its publishing channel."}},{"id":"069","slug":"zero-view-rate","category":"lab","term":"Zero-view rate","en":{"title":"How to Measure Your TikTok Zero-View Rate","dek":"Zero-view rate depends on observation age, measurement source and eligibility scope."}},{"id":"070","slug":"confidence-intervals","category":"lab","term":"Uncertainty","en":{"title":"Social Media Experiments: Confidence Intervals Explained","dek":"An interval expresses uncertainty under a method’s assumptions."}},{"id":"071","slug":"survivorship-bias","category":"lab","term":"Survivorship bias","en":{"title":"TikTok Case Studies and Survivorship Bias: What Is Missing?","dek":"Survivorship bias appears when analysis retains only still-visible units."}},{"id":"072","slug":"regression-to-mean","category":"lab","term":"Regression to the mean","en":{"title":"Why TikTok Views Drop After a Viral Post","dek":"An extreme outcome can be followed by more ordinary outcomes."}},{"id":"073","slug":"cohort-maturity","category":"lab","term":"Cohort maturity","en":{"title":"Campaign Cohort Analysis: Compare Equally Mature Results","dek":"Day-seven conversion should cover people given seven full days to convert."}},{"id":"074","slug":"attribution","category":"lab","term":"Attribution","en":{"title":"TikTok Marketing Attribution: UTMs, Visits and First Purchases","dek":"Campaign parameters describe an instrumented origin."}},{"id":"075","slug":"views-to-buyers","category":"lab","term":"Views to buyers","en":{"title":"From TikTok Views to Sales: Measure the Customer Journey","dek":"Views measure exposure under the platform’s definition."}},{"id":"076","slug":"experiment-preregistration","category":"lab","term":"Preregistration","en":{"title":"Social Media Experiment Template: Write the Plan First","dek":"Preregistering means recording an experiment’s question, criteria and planned analysis in advance."}},{"id":"077","slug":"stop-rules","category":"lab","term":"Stop rules","en":{"title":"When to Stop an AGD Experiment: Budget and Evidence Rules","dek":"A stop rule specifies when to end, pause or reconsider an experiment."}},{"id":"078","slug":"evidence-ladder","category":"lab","term":"Evidence ladder","en":{"title":"How to Evaluate AGD Claims: Documentation, Examples and Tests","dek":"The AGD evidence ladder separates platform documentation, methodical proprietary data, controlled experiments, repeated observations, hypotheses and folklore."}},{"id":"079","slug":"ai-agd","category":"machines","term":"AI AGD","en":{"title":"AI for AGD Marketing: From Creative Brief to Publishing Workflow","dek":"AI AGD means using AI to plan, produce, analyze or orchestrate AGD."}},{"id":"080","slug":"agentic-agd","category":"machines","term":"Agentic AGD","en":{"title":"Agentic AGD: What an AI Distribution Agent Should Do","dek":"Agentic AGD coordinates recurring decisions across accounts, content, markets and experiments."}},{"id":"081","slug":"human-api","category":"machines","term":"Human API","en":{"title":"TokPortal’s Human API: Briefs, Native Actions and Receipts","dek":"A Human API exposes a software workflow partly executed by people."}},{"id":"082","slug":"mcp-orchestration","category":"machines","term":"MCP orchestration","en":{"title":"TokPortal MCP Workflows: Connect AI to Social Operations","dek":"MCP lets an agent client discover and call tools exposed by a server."}},{"id":"083","slug":"dry-run-contract","category":"machines","term":"Dry-run contract","en":{"title":"What Does a TokPortal Dry Run Do? Preview Scope and Limits","dek":"A dry run validates a request without producing live effects under the service’s contract."}},{"id":"084","slug":"idempotency","category":"machines","term":"Idempotency","en":{"title":"API Retry Safety: Avoid Duplicate Social Publishing Operations","dek":"Idempotency prevents repeated execution of one intent from producing multiple effects when supported by the operation’s contract."}},{"id":"085","slug":"webhooks","category":"machines","term":"Webhooks","en":{"title":"Social Publishing Webhooks: Events, Status and Recovery","dek":"A webhook sends an event to your integration."}},{"id":"086","slug":"agent-budget","category":"machines","term":"Agent budgets","en":{"title":"How to Set a Budget for an AI Marketing Agent","dek":"An agent budget defines authorized operations, limits and renewal conditions."}},{"id":"087","slug":"agent-maturity","category":"machines","term":"AGD maturity model","en":{"title":"AI Marketing Automation: When to Increase Agent Autonomy","dek":"The AGD model distinguishes manual work, AI assistance, approved orchestration, agentic management and broader autonomy."}},{"id":"088","slug":"api-slop","category":"machines","term":"API Slop","en":{"title":"Social Media API Automation: Keep the Editorial Brief Intact","dek":"API Slop criticizes mass delivery of undifferentiated content without attention to accounts or context."}},{"id":"089","slug":"content-routing","category":"machines","term":"Content routing","en":{"title":"Content Routing for Multiple Social Accounts","dek":"Routing connects creative work to an account by audience, persona, market and purpose."}},{"id":"090","slug":"creative-clustering","category":"machines","term":"Creative clustering","en":{"title":"How to Organize Social Creative by Idea and Mechanism","dek":"Creative clustering groups content under chosen criteria."}},{"id":"091","slug":"anomaly-detection","category":"machines","term":"Anomaly detection","en":{"title":"Social Media Monitoring: Build Useful Operational Alerts","dek":"Anomaly detection flags deviation from a defined baseline."}},{"id":"092","slug":"human-review","category":"machines","term":"Human review","en":{"title":"Human Review for AI Content: Approve the Version That Ships","dek":"Useful human review exposes the action, consequences and evidence to check."}},{"id":"093","slug":"source-of-truth","category":"machines","term":"Source of truth","en":{"title":"Marketing Automation Records: Build a Reliable Source of Truth","dek":"A technical source of truth describes an interface’s current capabilities."}},{"id":"094","slug":"seo-agd","category":"machines","term":"SEO AGD","en":{"title":"AGD and SEO: Turn Social Ideas into Searchable Articles","dek":"SEO AGD explores social content and properties appearing in search engines and platform search."}},{"id":"095","slug":"pseo-agd","category":"machines","term":"pSEO AGD","en":{"title":"Programmatic SEO for AGD: Structure Useful, Distinct Pages","dek":"pSEO AGD systematically organizes social content around distinct search intents."}},{"id":"096","slug":"llm-quoting","category":"machines","term":"LLM quoting","en":{"title":"Writing AGD Content That Search and AI Can Cite","dek":"Citable content clearly states a proposition, scope and provenance."}},{"id":"097","slug":"knowledge-graph","category":"machines","term":"AGD content graph","en":{"title":"Internal Linking for AGD Content: Connect Concepts Clearly","dek":"An editorial graph connects parent concepts, neighbors and applications."}},{"id":"098","slug":"multilingual-seo","category":"machines","term":"Multilingual publishing","en":{"title":"Multilingual Content Strategy: When to Expand Your AGD Site","dek":"A multilingual publication gives each version a stable URL and connects matching translations."}},{"id":"099","slug":"structured-editorial","category":"machines","term":"Structured editorial","en":{"title":"AGD Article Schema: Structure Text, Stories and Real Examples","dek":"An editorial schema requires publishing essentials: identity, translations, media, stories, text, sources and links."}},{"id":"100","slug":"agent-audit-log","category":"machines","term":"Agent audit log","en":{"title":"AI Agent Audit Logs: Trace Marketing Actions and Decisions","dek":"An agent log connects intent, tool, result and next decision."}}]}],"$Lf","$L10"]}]
11:T56f,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"Article","@id":"https://theorganiclub.com/en/read/machines/mcp-orchestration/#article","headline":"TokPortal MCP Workflows: Connect AI to Social Operations","description":"MCP lets an agent client discover and call tools exposed by a server.","inLanguage":"en","datePublished":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","dateModified":"2026-09-09T07:41:56.167Z","image":["https://theorganiclub.com/images/editorial/mcp-orchestration.jpg"],"author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Jet","url":"https://theorganiclub.com/en/about/#jet","image":"https://theorganiclub.com/images/authors/jet.jpg"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"THE ORGANIC CLUB","url":"https://theorganiclub.com"},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://theorganiclub.com/en/read/machines/mcp-orchestration/","articleSection":"Machines & humans","wordCount":610,"citation":["https://developers.tokportal.com/mcp/","https://developers.tokportal.com/sandbox/"]},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"THE ORGANIC CLUB","item":"https://theorganiclub.com/en/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Machines & humans","item":"https://theorganiclub.com/en/topics/machines/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"TokPortal MCP Workflows: Connect AI to Social Operations","item":"https://theorganiclub.com/en/read/machines/mcp-orchestration/"}]}]}1:["$","main",null,{"id":"main","className":"main-shell","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$11"}}],["$","$L12",null,{"article":{"id":"082","slug":"mcp-orchestration","term":"MCP orchestration","category":"machines","kind":"guide","image":"mcp-orchestration","tier":"operating","evidence":"documented","sources":["https://developers.tokportal.com/mcp/"],"related":["dry-run-contract","human-api","distribution-is-the-moat"],"tokportal":"mcp","en":{"title":"TokPortal MCP Workflows: Connect AI to Social Operations","dek":"MCP lets an agent client discover and call tools exposed by a server.","point":"MCP lets an agent client discover and call tools exposed by a server. Its technical catalog still needs an objective and action boundaries.","body":["Read descriptions and annotations before composing a recipe. A read operation differs from paid creation. TokPortal’s documentation distinguishes local and remote servers. Choose transport for your environment and test the contract in preview before commercial execution.","A readable recipe names the intent before listing calls: prepare an account in a market, verify its state, organize publication. Each step should state what it requires from the previous one. Readers can then understand dependencies and see why synthetic preview identifiers must never pass into live operations. Tool availability is only one part of building a coherent, authorized workflow."],"action":["Discover the current catalog.","Separate read tools from mutations."],"trap":"A tool name is not enough to understand costs and side effects.","quote":"MCP connects tools. It does not write your strategy.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"MCP connects tools. It does not write your strategy.","text":"MCP lets an agent client discover and call tools exposed by a server.","media":"/images/editorial/mcp-orchestration.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"MCP orchestration","text":"MCP lets an agent client discover and call tools exposed by a server. Its technical catalog still needs an objective and action boundaries.","media":"/images/editorial/mcp-orchestration.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A tool name is not enough to understand costs and side effects.","media":"/images/editorial/mcp-orchestration.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Discover the current catalog.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/mcp-orchestration.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Separate read tools from mutations.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/mcp-orchestration.jpg"}]}]},"workshops":[{"id":"connect","title":"Connect an AI assistant to the actual TokPortal tools","intro":"The remote MCP address is the entry point for an assistant. The screenshot shows TokPortal’s real connection screen, including the authorisation step. Your API key does not belong in an editorial prompt.","endpoint":"https://app.tokportal.com/api/ext/mcp","code":"Inspect my existing TikTok accounts and the current credit rules.\nPrepare three distinct creative angles for a US audience.\nFor each, identify the account, required media and a valid publishing window.\nPreview any proposed creation with dry_run: true.\nReport credits_would_charge, recurring Coverage and missing inputs.\nDo not create or publish a live task.","language":"text","explain":"Copy this as a planning brief after connecting your assistant. It asks for a concrete preview, not a pretend transcript of successful execution. Remote MCP supports the documented dry-run workflow; local tokportal-mcp needs version 1.15.1 or later.","checks":[{"label":"Read-only first","detail":"Choose read-only access when the job is inventory or analysis. Publishing requires an appropriately authorised connection."},{"label":"Discover current tools","detail":"Use the tool catalogue available in the connected workspace instead of assuming a capability from a marketing page."},{"label":"Review before execution","detail":"Check destination, assets, price and review windows against the actual tool response."}],"sources":["https://developers.tokportal.com/mcp/"],"checkedAt":"2026-09-09T00:00:00Z","capture":{"src":"/images/tokportal/tokportal-mcp-connect.png","width":930,"height":250,"alt":"TokPortal connection screen with the remote MCP URL and Claude connection steps.","caption":"Actual TokPortal MCP connection screen, captured 8 September 2026.","source":"https://app.tokportal.com/developer/connect-ai"}},{"id":"preview","title":"Preview three TikTok uploads before committing credits","intro":"The builder makes the operational choices visible: a new account, its country and the number of uploads. The MCP request below expresses those same choices as a simulation.","endpoint":"POST /api/ext/bundles","code":"{\n  \"tool\": \"tokportal_create_bundle\",\n  \"arguments\": {\n    \"dry_run\": true,\n    \"body\": {\n      \"bundle_type\": \"account_and_videos\",\n      \"platform\": \"tiktok\",\n      \"country\": \"USA\",\n      \"videos_quantity\": 3,\n      \"edits_quantity\": 0,\n      \"wants_advanced_warming\": false,\n      \"auto_finalize_videos\": false\n    }\n  }\n}","language":"json","explain":"This is a sample request, not an executed order or a price quote. In REST, the equivalent simulation uses X-TokPortal-Dry-Run: true. Live creation debits credits immediately; the preview is the place to inspect the actual workspace-specific price.","checks":[{"label":"Read the quote","detail":"Inspect credits_would_charge and recurring Coverage. A dry run reports credits_charged as 0."},{"label":"Keep simulation separate","detail":"Returned simulation IDs are synthetic and cannot be reused in live requests. The simulation does not retain cross-call objects."},{"label":"Review the package","detail":"auto_finalize_videos is explicitly false here. Check the current review-window rules before any live execution."}],"sources":["https://developers.tokportal.com/sandbox/","https://developers.tokportal.com/mcp/"],"checkedAt":"2026-09-09T00:00:00Z","capture":{"src":"/images/tokportal/tokportal-bundle-builder.png","width":731,"height":655,"alt":"TokPortal bundle builder showing platform and account-plus-video choices.","caption":"Actual TokPortal builder, captured 8 September 2026.","source":"https://app.tokportal.com/bundles/create"}}],"schemaVersion":2,"deepDive":{"heading":"A tool catalogue is not an operating plan","paragraphs":["MCP makes tools discoverable to an assistant, but discoverability does not decide when a tool should be used. The orchestrator still needs to understand the account, the intended action, the input contract and the side effects. Read tool descriptions and current documentation before constructing a workflow. A list operation, a preview and a purchase may sit beside each other in the same catalogue while requiring different authority. Preserve that distinction in the plan and in the interface shown to the person approving consequential work.","Build the sequence around evidence returned by each step. Resolve identifiers before preparing an action, preview where supported, inspect cost and scope, then execute only the authorised operation. Store the resulting identifiers so later status checks refer to the same task. Do not infer success from a fluent assistant message or from the absence of a thrown error. A useful MCP integration makes the underlying operation easier to inspect. It should not hide uncertainty behind a conversational layer that sounds more complete than the tool response actually is."],"diagram":{"kind":"flow","title":"From discoverable tools to a reviewable action","items":[{"label":"Discover","detail":"Read the current tool contract and side effects.","value":0},{"label":"Prepare","detail":"Resolve inputs and inspect any supported preview.","value":0},{"label":"Reconcile","detail":"Store identifiers and verify the returned state.","value":0}],"caption":"Editorial model: a way to reason about the process, not measured platform results."},"caseLens":"The visible post is the end of a workflow. Tool orchestration needs its own operational evidence; the creative does not supply it.","caseIds":[]},"examples":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T07:41:56.167Z","author":"jet","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/mcp-orchestration.jpg","width":1280,"height":813,"alt":{"en":"Rows of terminals and connected wires on a telephone network patch panel."},"credit":"Dennis van Zuijlekom","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 48635187f29082eba162a0fa0936511cf975dcd3.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Krone_LSA-PLUS_Patch_Panel_(14672372192).png","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0"}},"lang":"en","next":{"id":"083","slug":"dry-run-contract","term":"Dry-run contract","category":"machines","kind":"guide","image":"dry-run-contract","tier":"operating","evidence":"documented","sources":["https://developers.tokportal.com/sandbox/"],"related":["idempotency","mcp-orchestration","distribution-is-the-moat"],"tokportal":"sandbox","en":{"title":"What Does a TokPortal Dry Run Do? Preview Scope and Limits","dek":"A dry run validates a request without producing live effects under the service’s contract.","point":"A dry run validates a request without producing live effects under the service’s contract. It does not guarantee future capacity or outcomes.","body":["In TokPortal MCP, dry_run belongs at the top argument level, not inside body. The local version must support that contract. Read response fields for simulated and actual charges. Preview identifiers remain synthetic: moving live requires creating and using actual resources.","Show the mode, request and reported charges in the human-readable result. Do not say account created when the service only validated a preview. That wording prevents another agent from continuing work against an imaginary resource. The boundary should be both technical and understandable in the report, especially when output is copied into another task without the full execution history attached."],"action":["Check version and preview response.","Keep an explicit boundary before live execution."],"trap":"A successful preview neither authorizes spending nor reserves capacity.","quote":"A preview must know what it does not simulate.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"A preview must know what it does not simulate.","text":"A dry run validates a request without producing live effects under the service’s contract.","media":"/images/editorial/dry-run-contract.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Dry-run contract","text":"A dry run validates a request without producing live effects under the service’s contract. It does not guarantee future capacity or outcomes.","media":"/images/editorial/dry-run-contract.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A successful preview neither authorizes spending nor reserves capacity.","media":"/images/editorial/dry-run-contract.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Check version and preview response.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/dry-run-contract.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Keep an explicit boundary before live execution.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/dry-run-contract.jpg"}]}]},"workshops":[{"id":"sandbox","title":"What the sandbox actually guarantees","intro":"The official sandbox page makes a useful boundary explicit: real request validation and pricing, with no created task or charge. This is an operational preview, not a simulation of TikTok reach.","endpoint":"POST /api/ext/bundles + X-TokPortal-Dry-Run: true","code":"{\n  \"dry_run\": true,\n  \"dry_run_notice\": \"<read the actual notice returned>\",\n  \"credits_would_charge\": \"<workspace-specific quote>\",\n  \"credits_charged\": 0\n}","language":"json","explain":"The fields shown are an annotated response shape. No live quote was requested for this article. Use the actual response from your connected workspace and keep any synthetic identifiers out of a live workflow.","checks":[{"label":"Validation","detail":"Invalid inputs still return real validation errors."},{"label":"Pricing","detail":"The quoted cost uses the same server-side pricing logic; the preview does not charge it."},{"label":"Distribution","detail":"A successful preview says nothing about the reach, retention or sales a future post will generate."}],"sources":["https://developers.tokportal.com/sandbox/"],"checkedAt":"2026-09-09T00:00:00Z","capture":{"src":"/images/tokportal/sandbox-docs.jpg","width":1280,"height":720,"alt":"Official TokPortal sandbox documentation explaining the dry-run header and simulated requests.","caption":"Public sandbox documentation, captured 9 September 2026.","source":"https://developers.tokportal.com/sandbox/"}}],"schemaVersion":2,"deepDive":{"heading":"A preview should answer the expensive questions","paragraphs":["A dry run is valuable when it shows what the live operation would target, create and cost without performing those side effects. Its contract should say which validations are real and which outcomes remain unknowable until execution. A preview that merely echoes the request can still be useful, but it must not be presented as proof that the live action will succeed. Inspect the documented response fields and retain the exact proposed inputs so the eventual approval refers to a concrete operation.","Bind the approved preview to the execution version. If the country, account, asset or quantity changes afterwards, the old preview no longer describes the new request. Recheck the fields that determine scope and cost before proceeding. Keep credentials out of logs and distinguish a preview identifier from a completed order identifier. For TokPortal, consult the current sandbox and MCP documentation for supported dry-run behaviour rather than assuming every tool has identical semantics. The point is to make consequences legible before execution and the eventual result traceable afterwards."],"diagram":{"kind":"timeline","title":"A preview is a versioned proposal","items":[{"label":"Prepare","detail":"Freeze the intended inputs and destination.","value":0},{"label":"Inspect","detail":"Review supported validation, scope and cost.","value":0},{"label":"Execute","detail":"Use the approved version and verify its result.","value":0}],"caption":"Editorial model: a way to reason about the process, not measured platform results."},"caseLens":"A polished creative preview and an operational dry run answer different questions. Both need to correspond to the version eventually released.","caseIds":[]},"examples":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T07:41:56.167Z","author":"jet","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/dry-run-contract.jpg","width":1280,"height":992,"alt":{"en":"Mary Jackson holds an aircraft model inside a wind tunnel at NASA Langley."},"credit":"NASA; restoration by Adam Cuerden","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 42976da6950d21d2f0ae93640659121b482a3bab.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mary_Jackson_in_a_wind_tunnel_with_a_model_at_NASA_Langley.jpg","license":"Public domain","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/"}},"previous":{"id":"081","slug":"human-api","term":"Human API","category":"machines","kind":"guide","image":"human-api","tier":"operating","evidence":"documented","sources":["https://developers.tokportal.com/"],"related":["mcp-orchestration","agentic-agd","distribution-is-the-moat"],"tokportal":"mcp","en":{"title":"TokPortal’s Human API: Briefs, Native Actions and Receipts","dek":"A Human API exposes a software workflow partly executed by people.","point":"A Human API exposes a software workflow partly executed by people. In TokPortal’s context, orchestration and native interaction are separate layers.","body":["A call may create a mission rather than immediately publish a post. Integrations therefore need waiting, status and correction handling. Design around the real cycle: request received, work executed, result verified. Hiding latency behind instant success misrepresents what happened.","A client interface can show request accepted before publication verified. Add handling for delays and corrections. This matters for agents: they should not analyze a mission as though it were already a visible post. The software contract should respect the actual time of human work. Clear intermediate states make integrations more useful without promising instantaneous execution the underlying operation does not provide."],"action":["Separate acceptance from delivery.","Plan status feedback and correction handling."],"trap":"A successful HTTP response can confirm request creation without confirming final execution.","quote":"Behind the API, someone actually opens the app.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Behind the API, someone actually opens the app.","text":"A Human API exposes a software workflow partly executed by people.","media":"/images/editorial/human-api.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Human API","text":"A Human API exposes a software workflow partly executed by people. In TokPortal’s context, orchestration and native interaction are separate layers.","media":"/images/editorial/human-api.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A successful HTTP response can confirm request creation without confirming final execution.","media":"/images/editorial/human-api.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Separate acceptance from delivery.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/human-api.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Plan status feedback and correction handling.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/human-api.jpg"}]}]},"workshops":[{"id":"video","title":"Prepare the actual video slot, not just the caption","intro":"TokPortal’s editor distinguishes Video, Carousel and Story, and asks for a target publishing period. The API follows the same operational idea: the content needs a valid format, accessible media and a usable window.","endpoint":"PUT /api/ext/bundles/{id}/videos/{position}","code":"{\n  \"tool\": \"tokportal_configure_bundle_video\",\n  \"arguments\": {\n    \"id\": \"<real-bundle-uuid>\",\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"body\": {\n      \"video_type\": \"video\",\n      \"video_url\": \"<public_url returned by your video upload>\",\n      \"description\": \"A practical example of organising freelance subscriptions.\",\n      \"target_publish_date\": \"<valid future date: YYYY-MM-DD>\"\n    }\n  }\n}","language":"json","explain":"Replace the marked values with your actual upload and bundle. This template is intentionally not a runnable campaign. target_publish_date starts a two-day publishing window; it does not request an exact minute.","checks":[{"label":"Choose the correct media fields","detail":"A video needs video_url and description. A TikTok carousel instead needs carousel_images and tiktok_sound_url."},{"label":"Use a valid window","detail":"Allow at least three days while account creation is pending, or one day for delivered/existing accounts. Check the current response and limits."},{"label":"Inspect readiness","detail":"GET /api/ext/bundles/{id}/publish-readiness lists blockers without a debit or mutation. Review ignored_fields and the returned start/end dates."}],"sources":["https://developers.tokportal.com/mcp/"],"checkedAt":"2026-09-09T00:00:00Z","capture":{"src":"/images/tokportal/tokportal-video-editor.png","width":650,"height":565,"alt":"Two real TokPortal editor views showing media format, caption and target publishing period.","caption":"Two cropped views of the real video editor, captured 8 September 2026. Historical dates shown; use a valid future window for a new task.","source":"https://app.tokportal.com/dashboard"}}],"schemaVersion":2,"deepDive":{"heading":"Make the handoff executable by a person","paragraphs":["A human operator is not a magic endpoint that repairs every vague request. If the task is to publish a post, the handoff needs an account identifier, approved asset, caption, timing constraints and a definition of completion. Include the relevant rights and any feature that must be applied inside the platform. Replace instructions such as make it feel native with concrete observations the operator can act on. The human's judgement should be reserved for real ambiguity, not spent guessing which file named final is actually approved.","Ask for evidence proportional to the operation. A public URL and completion timestamp may be enough for an ordinary post; a failed task needs a clear state and reason rather than a generic done message. Do not require screenshots containing unnecessary personal or account information. Keep a route for clarification and a rule against improvising outside the authorised scope. The advantage of a human handoff is contextual judgement where interfaces remain awkward. Treating the person as invisible glue makes that judgement difficult to review and the process difficult to improve."],"diagram":{"kind":"flow","title":"A useful operator contract","items":[{"label":"Input","detail":"Account, approved version and publishing constraints.","value":0},{"label":"Decision","detail":"Explicit room for judgement and escalation.","value":0},{"label":"Receipt","detail":"Result URL, time and any unresolved exception.","value":0}],"caption":"Editorial model: a way to reason about the process, not measured platform results."},"caseLens":"This post can illustrate a desired creative treatment. A usable handoff must still specify which elements to reproduce in an original asset.","caseIds":[]},"examples":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T07:41:56.167Z","author":"jet","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/human-api.jpg","width":1280,"height":960,"alt":{"en":"A worker operates an antique printing press inside a working print shop."},"credit":"Caelb375","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 2aa5baf9386557b730ec488a397287c9d71e5e4b.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Printing_at_Bay_View_Printing_Company.png","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"}}}],"$L13","$L14","$L15","$L16"]}]
